{"schema_version":"1.0","language":"en","edition":"en-ak","revision":"0","book":{"position":22,"code":"SNG","name":"Song of Songs","testament":"OT"},"chapter":4,"content":[{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"1","sid":"SNG 4:1"},"Behold, thou ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["art"]}," fair, my love; behold, thou ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["art "]},"fair; thou ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["hast"]}," doves’ eyes within thy locks: thy hair ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," as a flock of goats, that appear from mount Gilead. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 4:1"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"2","sid":"SNG 4:2"},"Thy teeth ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," like a flock ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["of sheep that are even "]},"shorn, which came up from the washing; whereof every one bear twins, and none ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," barren among them. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 4:2"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"3","sid":"SNG 4:3"},"Thy lips ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," like a thread of scarlet, and thy speech ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," comely: thy temples ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," like a piece of a pomegranate within thy locks. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 4:3"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"4","sid":"SNG 4:4"},"Thy neck ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," like the tower of David builded for an armoury, whereon there hang a thousand bucklers, all shields of mighty men. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 4:4"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"5","sid":"SNG 4:5"},"Thy two breasts ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," like two young roes that are twins, which feed among the lilies. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 4:5"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"6","sid":"SNG 4:6"},"Until the day break, and the shadows flee away, I will get me to the mountain of myrrh, and to the hill of frankincense. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 4:6"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"7","sid":"SNG 4:7"},"Thou ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["art"]}," all fair, my love; ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["there is"]}," no spot in thee. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 4:7"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"8","sid":"SNG 4:8"},"Come with me from Lebanon, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["my"]}," spouse, with me from Lebanon: look from the top of Amana, from the top of Shenir and Hermon, from the lions’ dens, from the mountains of the leopards. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 4:8"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"9","sid":"SNG 4:9"},"Thou hast ravished my heart, my sister, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["my"]}," spouse; thou hast ravished my heart with one of thine eyes, with one chain of thy neck. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 4:9"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"10","sid":"SNG 4:10"},"How fair is thy love, my sister, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["my"]}," spouse! how much better is thy love than wine! and the smell of thine ointments than all spices! ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 4:10"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"11","sid":"SNG 4:11"},"Thy lips, O ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["my"]}," spouse, drop ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["as"]}," the honeycomb: honey and milk ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," under thy tongue; and the smell of thy garments ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," like the smell of Lebanon. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 4:11"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"12","sid":"SNG 4:12"},"A garden inclosed ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," my sister, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["my"]}," spouse; a spring shut up, a fountain sealed. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 4:12"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"13","sid":"SNG 4:13"},"Thy plants ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," an orchard of pomegranates, with pleasant fruits; camphire, with spikenard, ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 4:13"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"14","sid":"SNG 4:14"},"Spikenard and saffron; calamus and cinnamon, with all trees of frankincense; myrrh and aloes, with all the chief spices: ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 4:14"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"15","sid":"SNG 4:15"},"A fountain of gardens, a well of living waters, and streams from Lebanon. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 4:15"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"16","sid":"SNG 4:16"},"Awake, O north wind; and come, thou south; blow upon my garden, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["that"]}," the spices thereof may flow out. Let my beloved come into his garden, and eat his pleasant fruits. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 4:16"}]}]}
